    tldr: "A protein that seals the gaps between stomach lining cells. It stays on many stomach cancers as they spread, and two approved treatments are given only to patients whose biopsy shows it.",
    summary:
      "Claudin-18 splice variant 2 is a tight-junction protein of the gastric mucosa whose epitope becomes accessible on tumour cells as normal tissue architecture breaks down, making it an unusually tractable target in a cancer with few. It is the selection biomarker for zolbetuximab, approved in the US, EU, Japan and China for CLDN18.2-positive, HER2-negative gastric and gastro-oesophageal junction adenocarcinoma, and in June 2026 China approved satricabtagene autoleucel, a CLDN18.2 CAR-T, in the same biomarker-defined population.\n\nPositivity depends entirely on where the threshold is set. Across 4,507 patients screened for the SPOTLIGHT and GLOW trials, 38.4% were positive at the label threshold of moderate-to-strong membranous staining in at least 75% of tumour cells, and the sponsor reports approximately 35% positivity in Chinese patients with advanced disease. Selection is performed with the VENTANA CLDN18 (43-14A) RxDx assay.\n\nThe assay's failure mode is sampling, and it has been quantified. Against whole-tumour-section ground truth a single representative biopsy gave 58.8% sensitivity, rising to 76.5% with six to eight biopsies, and a minimum of six endoscopic biopsies was needed to keep false negatives acceptably low; 18% of tumours were discordant between the primary and a matched nodal metastasis. A multi-laboratory ring trial found a 12% false-negative rate at 91% overall accuracy. That is the gap three Chinese groups are now trying to close with PET: 68Ga-PMD22, 68Ga-NC-BCH and 124I-18B10(10L) each have a published first-in-human pilot of 11 to 17 patients.",
